          "final_text_tail": "here in the header (skipped unconditionally, including right after the condition)\n- Parses the singular content block via `_parse_block()`\n- Optionally parses a `pluralize` block\n- **Mandatory** `fallback` block \u2014 raises `TemplateSyntaxError` \"expected 'fallback' block\" if missing\n- Raises `TemplateSyntaxError` \"unclosed conditional translation block\" on EOF\n- Raises `TemplateAssertionError` \"...defined twice.\" for duplicate variables\n- Respects `environment.policies[\"ext.i18n.trimmed\"]` for default trimming\n\n**`_make_conditional_node()` method:**\n- Builds a `nodes.If` node with the condition as the test expression\n- **True branch**: calls `gettext` (or `ngettext` when a plural form exists), handling both old-style (`Mod` node) and new-style (keyword arguments) formatting per `environment.newstyle_gettext`, wrapped in `MarkSafeIfAutoescape`\n- **False branch**: renders the fallback directly with `%`-style variable substitution (no gettext call), wrapped in `MarkSafeIfAutoescape`, with `%%` unescaped when no variables are used (keeping it consistent with the translation path)\n\n**Variable handling** supports both implicit variables (from `{{ var }}` in content) and explicit header assignments, creating `Name` nodes for undefined variables.\n\nAll 830 existing tests pass, and I verified the full feature set: conditional true/false rendering, pluralize\u2192ngettext, trimmed/notrimmed (applied to the fallback too), optional commas, autoescape, newstyle gettext, and all three error cases.",
